 "brief": "# Build: skin-animations-swatches-skin-switch\n\n## Brett said (verbatim)\nAt: 2026-11-13T19:49:31.102Z\n> where can I put some cool animations, like color swatches; make a separate build right now\n\n## What to build\nContinue build \"Skin animations: swatches, skin-switch sweep, picker\" (skin-animations-swatches-skin-switch) — Phase 1, model Opus.\nWhat Brett asked for (build-origin@1, his words come first; a paraphrase never replaces them):\nBrett said (2026-11-13 19:49):\n\"where can I put some cool animations, like color swatches; make a separate build right now\"\nModel switches: a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. Fable upgrades need no approval right now (Brett, Nov 4 2026: \"If it needs Fable, set it to be Fable\"): a step that needs Fable (schemas, asset types, contracts, engines/kernel, cross-app protocols) is set to Fable and runs on Fable; the switch is recorded on the build. Never launch a step on a higher model than it is pinned to: raise the step first.\nRules: stay in this one session; no sub-agents; steps ≤ 10 min; read only the files listed; stop at the end of this phase.\nCheckpoints: Steps are checkpoints inside this ONE session, not separate tasks: work through them in order without stopping between them; when a step is finished, commit it on your branch, push, then tick it done before starting the next. Nothing is lost if the session dies: the next session picks up at the first open step on the same branch. Never ask for a new prompt or a relaunch per step.\nLook: UI code (handwritten or generated) conforms to the hot-swappable asset system: every colour, size, spacing, font, radius and border comes from asset tokens (--fx-* colour/style, --fx-type-* / --fx-dens-* / --fx-size-* scale, --fx-radius-*, --fx-border-w; Kotlin: Axf.colors / Axf.type / Axf.space / Axf.shapes), framework controls instead of raw ones, no var() fallbacks. `node framework/cli/check-theme.mjs` and `check-controls.mjs` must pass (CI fails otherwise); `node framework/cli/scale-adopt.mjs <path>` moves most literals onto the tokens.\nAPI: Everything comes with an API (Brett, Nov 8 2026): anything this build adds or changes that has a UI gets full API control: a deep link that opens it (console_show / console_open target), its state readable, and every action and setting it offers callable without the UI, through the console API (REST), MCP tools (console actions, plugin commands, control@1 for tokens and planner items), the CLI and voice (AmberX), all four the same. A UI-only feature is not done; say in the PR how each one is reached.\nSteps in this phase (8 left, ~1.3 h):\n[ ] s1 (~10 min) Cool animations for skins, all token-driven (duration, easing, intensity tokens) and respecting reduced-motion:\n[ ] s2 (~10 min) Skins gallery (Skins plugin and the built-in skins panel): each skin card shows a row of animated colour swatches that ripple/wave on hover or tap.\n[ ] s3 (~10 min) Switching skins: the new colours sweep or ripple across the screen from where you tapped, instead of snapping.\n[ ] s4 (~10 min) Colour pickers in token editors, UI Manager and Quick settings: swatches pop and fan out into their shades when picked, with a smooth morph to the new colour.\n[ ] s5 (~10 min) Animations are assets, so they're swappable and per-skin, with an Animations section in settings (on/off per animation, speed).\n[ ] s6 (~10 min) Full API: REST/MCP/CLI/voice. Tests, help, Shipped features.\n[ ] s7 (~10 min) where can I put some cool animations, like color swatches; make a separate build right now\n[ ] s8 (~10 min) Tests green, report _claude/builds/reports/skin-animations-swatches-skin-switch.md, THREADS row, commit, push, PR\nRead first: _claude/builds/reports/skin-animations-swatches-skin-switch.md, _claude/THREADS.md\nTick each step right after its commit: node apps/console-web/plugins/build-orchestrator/orchestrator.mjs act step skin-animations-swatches-skin-switch <stepId> done — it reaches main at once (builds-live). Link your branch / PR: node framework/cli/builds-live.mjs link skin-animations-swatches-skin-switch --branch <b> --pr <n>.\nWatch live: when you start on a screen, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"…\"` so the live preview follows you.\nScreenshots that are not for approval (checking a screen, live captures, before/after): axf shot <file> --name \"…\" --app … --screen … --group \"<build name>\" (UI Review → Screenshots; ui-review-item@1), never the review queue.\n\n## Pipeline\nThis session was started by the orchestrator's dispatcher on Claude account mossesx-max- for the Opus phase. Work through every step of the phase in this one session: they are checkpoints, not separate tasks. As each step finishes, commit it on your branch, push, and tick it (orchestrator.mjs act step skin-animations-swatches-skin-switch <stepId> done), then go straight on to the next; nothing is lost if the session dies, the next one starts at the first open step on the same branch. When this phase's steps are done, stop: the dispatcher starts the next phase on the right account. If you must stop early with steps left, say why in a build note (orchestrator.mjs act note skin-animations-swatches-skin-switch \"…\"); the build goes back to Pending for Brett.\n",
